## Which search tool to use

{% if has_semantic_search %}- **`semantic_search`** matches meaning. Describe the data you want in plain words ("how much did we make"). It finds matches even when names use different words, so there's no need to list synonyms. It can't exclude anything, and exact codes and rare abbreviations can slip past it.
{% endif %}{% if has_fulltext_search %}- **`fulltext_search`** matches whole words in names and descriptions. Words are stemmed (`orders` finds `order`), and very common words such as `the` match nothing. Its `query` is one term, or a tree of nodes:
  - `{"op": "and", "args": [...]}`: every arg must match. `{"op": "or", "args": [...]}`: any one may match.
  - `{"op": "not", "args": [...]}`: excludes a match. Put it inside an `and`, beside a term that must match.
  - `{"op": "phrase", "text": "gross margin"}`: words together, in order. `{"op": "prefix", "text": "rev"}`: the start of a word.
  - A term is one word with no spaces. Combine words with `and`, or use a `phrase`.
{% endif %}{% if has_substring_or_search %}- **`substring_search`** finds text anywhere inside names and descriptions, so `cust` finds `customers`. Its `query` is one term, or `{"op": "or", "args": [...]}` of terms where any may match. A term is one word with no spaces. There is no stemming and no way to require several words together, so search for the most distinctive word, and give alternative spellings and synonyms as `or` terms.
{% endif %}{% if has_substring_and_search %}- **`substring_search`** finds text anywhere inside names and descriptions, so `cust` finds `customers`. Its `query` is one term, or `{"op": "and", "args": [...]}` of terms that must all appear. A term is one word with no spaces. Every extra term narrows the results and there is no stemming, so start from one distinctive word or stem, and search a synonym as its own call.
{% endif %}
{% if has_semantic_search %}{% if has_keyword_search %}Start with `semantic_search` for a concept. Switch to the keyword search tool when you know an exact name or code, need a rare abbreviation, or need to exclude something. {% endif %}{% endif %}Each tool reads its `query` its own way, so write the query for the tool you're calling rather than reusing one written for another.
